<title>EGYPT: Egypt impounds Ukrainian ship for unpaid dues.</title>
<headline>Egypt impounds Ukrainian ship for unpaid dues.</headline>
<dateline>CAIRO 1996-12-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Egyptian authorities have impounded a Ukrainian cargo ship in the Red Sea port of Suez after its owners failed to pay $1 million to a local shipping agent, shipping sources said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>The agent, Bancomar, got a legal order to confiscate the ship after the owners, Black Sea Shipping Co., stopped paying accumulated dues for transit tolls and provisions, they added.</p>
<p>Svetlogorsk, with a gross-weight of 8,874 tonnes, was carrying general merchandise from the Gulf when it was impounded.</p>
</text>
